We can locate the first set bit using `stdc_trailing_zeros` (from C23 `<stdbit.h>`) and perform a modulo 8 operation:

```c
#include <stdbit.h>

// winning_moves is a bitboard showing where a player can win
int column = stdc_trailing_zeros(winning_moves) % 8;
```

**Explanation:** 
In a row-major layout, row $r$ starts at bit $8r$. A bit in column $c$ has index $8r + c$. Performing modulo 8 removes the row multiplier ($8r$), leaving the exact column index $c$ ($0 \le c \le 6$).
